# Code comments

- **User comments are sacred:** Never delete comments the user wrote (or that were already in the file from the user / prior work). You **may** modify, rephrase, translate, or relocate them so they stay accurate with the code. Do **not** strip them “for cleanup.”
- **When the agent may add comments:** Do **not** invent new comments from scratch without permission. Add a **new** comment only if the user explicitly asks. Improving an existing user comment (wording, English, accuracy) does not require a separate ask.
- **Exception:** Required lint suppressions (`biome-ignore` with a short reason on the line immediately above the diagnostic) are allowed when needed to pass the quality gate.
- **Language:** English only. If any Russian comments are introduced or found, replace them with an English translation (that counts as modifying, not deleting).
- **Purpose:** Explain *why* / non-obvious intent, constraints, or trade-offs — not *what* the next line does.
- **Avoid:** Narrating obvious code; large blocks of commented-out code; redundant JSDoc that only restates the name or types.
- **When a comment is warranted (if asked):** Non-obvious business rules, workarounds, security/auth caveats, tricky async/effect ordering, temporary test gates.
- **JSDoc:** Prefer for exported public APIs when behavior is not clear from the signature; keep short; use English — only when the user asks or when improving existing docs.
- **TODO/FIXME:** `// TODO: <actionable note>` (English); include context, not vague “fix later” — only when the user asks or when improving an existing TODO.
